  "result": "I wrote the test file at `tests/unit/intervals.test.ts`. When I ran `npx vitest run`, **13 tests passed and 4 failed**. The failures point to a bug in `mergeIntervals`, not in the tests.\n\n**The bug:** the comment on the function says it should \"merge every pair of blocks that overlaps **or touches**,\" with no two output blocks touching. But the check at `src/intervals.ts:17` is `start < last[1]`, so blocks that only share an endpoint stay separate. For example, `[[1, 2], [2, 3]]` comes back as `[[1, 2], [2, 3]]` instead of `[[1, 3]]`.\n\nThe 4 failing tests all check that touching blocks get merged:\n- merges intervals that touch at an endpoint\n- merges a chain of touching intervals into one\n- merges a zero-length interval touching another (`[1,3]` + `[3,3]`)\n- produces sorted output where no two intervals touch or overlap\n\n**The 13 passing tests cover:** empty input, a single block, separate blocks, overlapping blocks, one block inside another, a later block that ends earlier not shortening the result, unsorted input, zero-length blocks, duplicates, negative numbers, the input not being changed, and new block objects being returned.\n\nAs you asked, I didn't change `src/intervals.ts`. Changing `<` to `<=` on line 17 should make all 17 tests pass. If touching blocks are actually meant to stay separate, then the comment is what's wrong, and I'd update those 4 tests to match.",
